# Switcheroo: "Exchange control of two target creatures." When control of two permanents controlled by different players
# is exchanged, each player gains control of the one the other controlled, at once (CR 701.12b, 613.1b), with no end.
# Bot1's Ornithopter becomes Bot2's and Bot2's Llanowar Elves becomes Bot1's. Each came under its new controller this turn,
# so Bot1 can't tap the Elves for mana (CR 302.6); on Bot1's next turn it can, and the exchange has not ended.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Island
Ornithopter
Switcheroo
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Forest x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Switcheroo.Cast
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter; Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.SummoningSick = true
! Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Activate
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Activate
? Bot1.Mana = {G}

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Sapphire; Mox Jet; Mox Ruby; Mox Pearl; Island; Llanowar Elves
Bot1.Graveyard = Switcheroo
Bot2.Battlefield = Forest; Ornithopter
